  "question": {
    "html": "<p>A <span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"0.50\\text{ kg}\"></span> block of a pure substance is heated from its solid state by an electric heater of constant power. The following data table shows the variation of the temperature of the substance with time.</p>\n<table><thead><tr><th>Time / <span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"\\text{s}\"></span></th><th>Temperature / <span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"^\\circ\\text{C}\"></span></th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>0</td><td>10</td></tr><tr><td>60</td><td>30</td></tr><tr><td>120</td><td>50</td></tr><tr><td>180</td><td>50</td></tr><tr><td>240</td><td>50</td></tr><tr><td>300</td><td>80</td></tr><tr><td>360</td><td>110</td></tr></tbody></table>\n<p>What is the value of the ratio <span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"\\frac{\\text{specific heat capacity of the solid phase}}{\\text{specific heat capacity of the liquid phase}}\"></span>?</p><ol class=\"mcq-options\"><li data-label=\"A\"><p><span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"0.67\"></span></p></li><li data-label=\"B\"><p><span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"1.50\"></span></p></li><li data-label=\"C\"><p><span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"2.20\"></span></p></li><li data-label=\"D\"><p><span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"3.00\"></span></p></li></ol>"
